      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Noslan Ruiz-Bernal, of Cuba, was convicted of armed burglary in 2014 right after receiving his green card. He served just over a year in jail  and was released back into the community after his incarceration.\n\nMore recently, he was arrested for armed  burglary again, but this time by Broward County, Fla., law enforcement — a 287(g) partner. \n\nBroward County honored ICE’s detainer and handed him over to federal officers rather than releasing back into the community to reoffend — something sanctuary jurisdictions are unwilling to do.\n\n💻Learn more about the 287(g) program and ICE detainers on our website.",
      "text_resolved": "Noslan Ruiz-Bernal, of Cuba, was convicted of armed burglary in 2014 right after receiving his green card. He served just over a year in jail  and was released back into the community after his incarceration.\n\nMore recently, he was arrested for armed  burglary again, but this time by Broward County, Fla., law enforcement — a 287(g) partner. \n\nBroward County honored ICE’s detainer and handed him over to federal officers rather than releasing back into the community to reoffend — something sanctuary jurisdictions are unwilling to do.\n\n💻Learn more about the 287(g) program and ICE detainers on our website.",
